<div class="sop-callout">
  <strong>The 4-hour ceiling</strong>
  <p>The whole calendar is sized to a deliberate 4-hour daily working ceiling on this business. Five days a week, four hours each, plus a 60-minute Sunday social-content batch. That's <strong>21 hours a week of agency time, total</strong>, every week. Every cadence below fits inside that ceiling; nothing on this page assumes a longer day. If a new rhythm is going to be added, something else has to come out.</p>
  <p style="margin-top:0.65rem">Want the visual version? <a href="/sop/planner/">Open the planner</a> &mdash; year, quarter, month, week, and day views of these same rhythms.</p>
</div>

<h2>How to read this page</h2>

<p>Every other SOP in this portal owns a specific cadence: cold outreach runs Mondays, the newsletter ships every other Friday, QBRs are quarterly, etc. The cadences are documented inside each SOP, which is correct &mdash; the SOP that owns the work also owns its rhythm. But it leaves a gap: when I'm planning a week, a month, or a quarter, I need to see all the rhythms together so I can confirm nothing is colliding and nothing is forgotten.</p>

<p>This page is that view. Yearly down to daily, with explicit cross-references back to the SOP that owns each rhythm. Use it as the master calendar; treat the individual SOPs as the source of truth for how each rhythm runs.</p>

